description:
The doc comment on the ready handler (src/server/mod.rs:418-420) says:

    /// Note this currently reports only whether the store is *open*. A writer that has been
    /// **fenced**, or a reader that is arbitrarily **stale**, still reports ready — see
    /// `nidus-lp4.1`, which owns those.

Every clause of that is now false. The function body directly beneath it (src/server/mod.rs:429-450) checks status.fenced and returns 503, then checks staleness against max_staleness and returns 503. nidus-lp4.1 is closed, and e2e tests (fenced_writer_reports_unready, stale_reader_reports_unready, a_superseded_writer_discovers_it_is_fenced_without_any_write) assert exactly the behaviour the comment denies.

Filed rather than fixed in passing because the class of defect earned it. This session lost an entire investigation pass to stale metadata: nidus-lp4.7's notes described a "remaining second defect" that had already been fixed, and pointed at evidence gathered before the fix landed. Six further issues (lp4.1-.5 and the whole nidus-1e6 epic) were sitting open having shipped in merged PRs. A comment that confidently describes the opposite of the code beneath it is the same failure mode, and it sits on a security- and availability-relevant probe where a reader is most likely to trust it.

Worth a sweep rather than a single edit: check the other doc comments touched by the nidus-lp4 epic for the same drift, particularly anything that names an issue ID as "owning" future work, since those IDs are now closed.
